1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
Last time on Zombieland Saga Revenge, we somehow got back into doing the idol thing.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,500
It started with a TV appearance where we co-hosted a segment with Saga's very own rock star, White Ryu.

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:10,500
Can you believe?

4
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:13,500
Saki is a longtime fan of his, so she kind of went nuts.

5
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:15,500
It might even be love. Oh my gosh!

6
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:19,500
Then Saki found out that Ryu's radio show might be ending, and she went even more nuts!

7
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:22,500
She confessed her feelings to him, and he opened up to her, too.

8
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:23,500
It was super touching!

9
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:27,500
And now Frank Shishu is in charge of his radio show, so Saga can be Saga!

10
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:31,000
We're gonna light the way for Saga's burning soul!

11
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Such super tight choreography.

12
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,000
We're probably not at that level.

13
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:14,000
I think Kotaro's getting out of the bath now, so...

14
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:15,000
What's wrong?

15
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,000
There's nothing wrong at all!

16
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:18,000
I'm done!

17
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,000
So what kind of stuff were you looking up?

18
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,500
Just random things.

19
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:25,500
Hey, don't eat that!

20
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:26,500
It's not a thing!

21
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:27,500
That's for...

22
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:28,500
That's for...

23
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:29,500
Crap time!

24
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:30,500
Drop it!

25
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:32,200
We're already exactly right.

26
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:33,000
Those people...

27
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Whatever I say!

28
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Why would you be thinking about this hair?

29
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Something that she likes talking about?

30
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Things that usually look pretty tough, nobody does.

31
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,000
They would not have seen one thought.

32
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,000
But what kind of stuff that you tell people the first thought is?

33
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,000
What kind of stuff do you try to do?

34
00:03:00,972 --> 00:03:07,032
A show at 6-5-6, and we're on the radio!

35
00:03:07,712 --> 00:03:09,012
We hope you'll be there.

36
00:03:09,792 --> 00:03:10,672
Thank you.

37
00:03:12,132 --> 00:03:14,712
It feels like we're starting to make real progress.

38
00:03:17,312 --> 00:03:19,352
The schedule sure is filling up, huh?

39
00:03:19,932 --> 00:03:22,692
Half of these dates are for our part-time jobs, but yeah.

40
00:03:22,932 --> 00:03:27,392
Hell, if we're paying off our debt and doing idle stuff at the same time, we're on our way to Easy Street.

41
00:03:27,712 --> 00:03:29,072
Nope, not even close.

42
00:03:30,972 --> 00:03:38,272
If we start thinking we can relax now, then all we'll ever be known for is the time we bombed.

43
00:03:48,932 --> 00:03:53,572
We need to put the past behind us, find a way to rise above everyone's expectations.

44
00:03:54,432 --> 00:03:57,692
And if we can't, then we might as well be dead and buried.

45
00:03:57,692 --> 00:04:03,452
She's got a point. The entertainment industry's always been a cutthroat competition.

46
00:04:04,092 --> 00:04:06,272
And to fall behind is to die.

47
00:04:06,272 --> 00:04:18,712
I can't say no to a challenge.

48
00:04:18,932 --> 00:04:20,292
Right, let's advance.

49
00:04:20,692 --> 00:04:22,312
Better count me and two!

50
00:04:23,932 --> 00:04:24,992
Come on, Ty!

51
00:04:26,992 --> 00:04:28,252
I's exactly right.

52
00:04:28,972 --> 00:04:31,392
We have to keep growing and moving forward.

53
00:04:31,392 --> 00:04:33,712
Thank you for supporting the group!

54
00:04:33,992 --> 00:04:35,972
Number three is so inspirational!

55
00:04:36,312 --> 00:04:38,652
Yeah, you can tell she puts her all into it!

56
00:04:39,152 --> 00:04:39,472
Question.

57
00:04:39,972 --> 00:04:41,112
Which one looks better?

58
00:04:41,332 --> 00:04:41,632
Watch.

59
00:04:41,952 --> 00:04:44,112
Arm pointed out to the side or kind of downward?

60
00:04:44,772 --> 00:04:45,272
Real quick.

61
00:04:45,612 --> 00:04:47,652
I put together the intro for tomorrow's show.

62
00:04:47,772 --> 00:04:49,012
Could you look it over for me?

63
00:04:49,232 --> 00:04:52,692
I can't decide which one of these hair pieces would make me cuter!

64
00:04:52,812 --> 00:04:53,712
Let me see here.

65
00:04:53,712 --> 00:04:58,452
Either, both, doesn't matter.

66
00:05:04,092 --> 00:05:05,872
Ai, can you please tell me what to do?

67
00:05:05,932 --> 00:05:07,412
Ai, can I ask you for something?

68
00:05:07,732 --> 00:05:09,112
Ai, do you have just a second?

69
00:05:09,432 --> 00:05:10,372
Ai, help!

70
00:05:10,372 --> 00:05:10,792
Ah!

71
00:05:12,932 --> 00:05:13,892
Sakura center.

72
00:05:14,432 --> 00:05:16,352
Junko and Lily, you'll be on the right side.

73
00:05:16,492 --> 00:05:18,532
And Saki and Yugiri, you go on the left.

74
00:05:19,252 --> 00:05:20,432
Back a bit more.

75
00:05:20,432 --> 00:05:28,052
Iron Frill is coming here.

76
00:05:28,392 --> 00:05:30,752
Iron Frill is coming here.

77
00:05:31,092 --> 00:05:33,792
So get your zombie butts in here.

78
00:05:34,652 --> 00:05:35,532
Let's go!

79
00:05:35,732 --> 00:05:36,432
It's a raid!

80
00:05:36,612 --> 00:05:37,132
An ambush!

81
00:05:37,472 --> 00:05:38,132
They're coming!

82
00:05:38,992 --> 00:05:40,432
You little guy!

83
00:05:46,272 --> 00:05:46,912
Inai!

84
00:05:47,192 --> 00:05:49,392
You are to respond with a sir, yes, sir!

85
00:05:49,392 --> 00:05:54,832
You're just a bunch of wet corpses wallowing around in muck!

86
00:05:56,552 --> 00:05:58,712
No, you're the maggots that ate the corpses!

87
00:05:59,092 --> 00:06:00,172
Would you calm down?

88
00:06:00,552 --> 00:06:01,712
Get back to Iron Frill.

89
00:06:03,352 --> 00:06:06,932
Get the shit out of your ears and listen up, you shamble and sacks of bones!

90
00:06:07,572 --> 00:06:11,452
There's about to be another landmark added to the fierce battlefield that is Saga.

91
00:06:11,932 --> 00:06:13,392
The new Saga Arena!

92
00:06:14,192 --> 00:06:15,012
Wait, the what now?

93
00:06:15,012 --> 00:06:17,172
And guess who's breaking it in first?

94
00:06:17,472 --> 00:06:18,792
Iron Frill, obviously!

95
00:06:19,512 --> 00:06:19,852
Huh?

96
00:06:20,272 --> 00:06:24,152
Now, why is a big-time idol group from Tokyo being brought in for the inaugural performance

97
00:06:24,152 --> 00:06:26,232
at a venue in Little Old Saga, you may ask?

98
00:06:26,392 --> 00:06:28,592
And to that I say, who freaking knows?

99
00:06:29,052 --> 00:06:32,732
The important takeaway is that I found a way to weasel you maggots in as the opening air!

100
00:06:32,732 --> 00:06:38,472
You and those are going to be so awesome that those Tokyo are going to leave here not to shame!

101
00:06:38,672 --> 00:06:39,732
It's the perfect plan!

102
00:06:39,852 --> 00:06:41,052
So memorize it!

103
00:06:41,052 --> 00:06:42,112
You're kidding!

104
00:06:42,692 --> 00:06:43,752
The Iron Frill?

105
00:06:49,212 --> 00:06:49,852
Good!

106
00:06:53,392 --> 00:06:54,972
We can handle this!

107
00:06:55,612 --> 00:06:56,672
I know it!

108
00:06:57,972 --> 00:06:58,992
You're right!

109
00:07:00,892 --> 00:07:04,412
Yeah, lovely parade and all, but here comes the rain.

110
00:07:04,732 --> 00:07:06,052
Number three's not performing.

111
00:07:06,472 --> 00:07:06,792
What?

112
00:07:07,192 --> 00:07:07,512
Why?

113
00:07:07,512 --> 00:07:08,372
Oh?

114
00:07:08,812 --> 00:07:10,672
Did all your brains finally leak out?

115
00:07:11,192 --> 00:07:15,272
Iron Frill's famously deceased leader wants to flaunt her undeadliness right in front of

116
00:07:15,272 --> 00:07:15,892
her old group?

117
00:07:17,032 --> 00:07:21,232
We've been up in Saga's grill for months and we never worried about getting recognized before!

118
00:07:21,312 --> 00:07:24,232
Yeah, and we performed in the same stage as them back at Saga Rock!

119
00:07:24,292 --> 00:07:26,952
Please, we can't go on without Ai after coming this far!

120
00:07:27,232 --> 00:07:29,792
Froschuchu isn't Froschuchu if we're not singing together!

121
00:07:29,852 --> 00:07:33,132
Respect my authority or you'll run laps till your legs fall off again!

122
00:07:33,552 --> 00:07:35,712
As for you, we've got some solo gigs lined up.

123
00:07:35,712 --> 00:07:37,712
You'll be starting first thing tomorrow.

124
00:07:38,292 --> 00:07:38,972
At least!

125
00:07:41,712 --> 00:07:43,292
That didn't go too well.

126
00:07:45,972 --> 00:07:47,052
So what now?

127
00:07:48,932 --> 00:07:50,872
There's no reasoning with that guy.

128
00:07:52,072 --> 00:07:56,412
I'm sure one of us would have had to sit out eventually due to an injury or something like that.

129
00:07:56,892 --> 00:08:00,852
Maybe this is an opportunity for each member of Froschuchu to get a bit stronger.

130
00:08:01,252 --> 00:08:04,212
But it'll make me sad if you're the only person who's left out!

131
00:08:04,212 --> 00:08:05,512
Well, it's just this once.

132
00:08:05,872 --> 00:08:07,072
We want revenge, right?

133
00:08:07,232 --> 00:08:09,012
So we'll do whatever it takes to get it.

134
00:08:10,752 --> 00:08:11,232
Junko?

135
00:08:11,712 --> 00:08:13,532
I'm counting on you to take charge.

136
00:08:13,972 --> 00:08:16,712
After me, you're the most experienced idol we've got.

137
00:08:16,792 --> 00:08:17,232
Ugh.

138
00:08:20,432 --> 00:08:20,812
Right!

139
00:08:20,812 --> 00:08:32,952
All right!

140
00:08:33,072 --> 00:08:35,812
Today's special guest is number three from Froschuchu!

141
00:08:36,052 --> 00:08:36,312
Yay!

142
00:08:37,152 --> 00:08:37,372
Woo!

143
00:08:37,832 --> 00:08:38,252
Hey!

144
00:08:38,512 --> 00:08:40,212
I'm so happy to be here!

145
00:08:42,212 --> 00:08:42,652
Huh?

146
00:08:43,432 --> 00:08:45,992
I guess number three's doing solo stuff these days.

147
00:08:45,992 --> 00:08:48,452
I hope she's not breaking away from the gang.

148
00:08:48,812 --> 00:08:55,032
So I have to ask, has anyone ever told you that you bear a striking resemblance to the late Ai Mizuno from Iron Thrill?

149
00:08:56,192 --> 00:08:58,652
Yes, I do get that from time to time, actually.

150
00:08:59,032 --> 00:09:01,812
She was a legendary idol who people still admire.

151
00:09:02,272 --> 00:09:04,192
So I always consider it a compliment.

152
00:09:04,192 --> 00:09:17,772
They want you in Fukuoka for a live event, plus the Nagasaki Hydrangea Festival, and Beppu Hot Springs Hell, too.

153
00:09:18,152 --> 00:09:19,492
Now let me see here.

154
00:09:20,112 --> 00:09:22,692
Why don't you take those offers and shove them up, you buds?

155
00:09:22,752 --> 00:09:23,772
What were you doing?

156
00:09:24,112 --> 00:09:26,932
Froschuchu was created for Saga and Saga alone.

157
00:09:27,292 --> 00:09:31,632
Anyone else who wants you is merely trying to capitalize on Saga's glory.

158
00:09:31,972 --> 00:09:33,052
So trust no one.

159
00:09:33,052 --> 00:09:35,652
I've never heard you say that before.

160
00:09:37,592 --> 00:09:39,132
Are you plotting something?

161
00:09:41,232 --> 00:09:44,492
Why would you want to split us up at such an important time?

162
00:09:45,712 --> 00:09:48,372
We can't afford to fail this next performance.

163
00:09:49,452 --> 00:09:50,832
Just think about it.

164
00:09:51,032 --> 00:09:52,932
If it turns out like EFS did.

165
00:09:53,212 --> 00:09:56,632
Oh, honey, Froschuchu can get along perfectly well without you.

166
00:09:57,272 --> 00:09:59,312
Besides, you left Junko in charge, right?

167
00:09:59,812 --> 00:10:00,492
What's wrong?

168
00:10:00,492 --> 00:10:01,612
You don't trust her?

169
00:10:01,612 --> 00:10:06,392
Junko made it as a solo idol back in the 80s, when that was almost impossible to do.

170
00:10:06,832 --> 00:10:09,892
And they've all been working so hard to get over the EFS disaster.

171
00:10:10,292 --> 00:10:11,912
I'm sure that they can pull through.

172
00:10:12,432 --> 00:10:14,432
It sounds like to me everything's pagey!

173
00:10:14,432 --> 00:10:21,352
So if you just unclench your undead job for five minutes to focus on your solo career, and paying off this debt, we'd live happily ever after!

174
00:10:21,352 --> 00:10:25,212
How am I supposed to do any of that if you keep on turning down offers for dumb reasons?

175
00:10:25,212 --> 00:10:35,492
Everyone's been working so hard to learn the new choreo.

176
00:10:35,492 --> 00:10:40,672
But we're nowhere near the level we should be if we want to impress the fans coming to see Iron Frill.

177
00:10:41,272 --> 00:10:43,232
We just have to push ourselves.

178
00:10:43,232 --> 00:10:48,332
The concert will be here before we know it.

179
00:10:48,332 --> 00:10:51,552
If we don't nail this performance, we're going to bomb again!

180
00:10:52,792 --> 00:10:53,272
Junko?

181
00:10:54,012 --> 00:10:55,112
Uh, Junko?

182
00:10:55,452 --> 00:10:55,852
Uh...

183
00:10:55,852 --> 00:10:57,812
Did we do better that time?

184
00:10:57,952 --> 00:11:00,612
I feel like we're still a little too stiff in some parts.

185
00:11:01,252 --> 00:11:05,152
We should definitely go over it a couple more times, but you guys are doing a great job.

186
00:11:05,292 --> 00:11:06,212
Hell yeah! Rock!

187
00:11:06,212 --> 00:11:10,572
You just stared at us all creepy with your mouth open, so I wasn't sure how you felt about it.

188
00:11:11,092 --> 00:11:13,512
This concert is a big deal for Franshu Shuu!

189
00:11:13,672 --> 00:11:16,112
We've got this, man! We've got this by the ass!

190
00:11:17,192 --> 00:11:21,212
Let's focus on one thing at a time before we start getting too excited, okay, ladies?

191
00:11:21,752 --> 00:11:25,172
Yeah, I keep flailing my arms too much, and it's knocking my mic loose.

192
00:11:25,192 --> 00:11:28,632
That's because you're forgetting the choreo and making up your own dance moves.

193
00:11:28,632 --> 00:11:31,672
You seem troubled by something.

194
00:11:33,132 --> 00:11:35,232
I don't think you should be doing this right now.

195
00:11:35,872 --> 00:11:37,272
I'm so sorry, sir!

196
00:11:38,032 --> 00:11:39,472
Maybe you should call it a day.

197
00:11:58,632 --> 00:11:59,512
I'm back!

198
00:12:02,592 --> 00:12:03,772
Oh, hey there, Tai.

199
00:12:04,452 --> 00:12:06,292
Is everyone else still off at work?

200
00:12:06,492 --> 00:12:10,192
Up next is Franshu Shuu's number three singing Awaken Returner.

201
00:12:10,192 --> 00:12:34,692
If she'd been alive during my time in the 80s, I bet she could have become a top idol, maybe even as a solo artist.

202
00:12:34,692 --> 00:12:39,852
I have got to get out of this funk.

203
00:12:39,852 --> 00:12:55,892
Would you like to share your thoughts on the Saga Arena concert that's coming up this weekend?

204
00:12:56,352 --> 00:12:59,672
Of course! We think it's gonna be a super incredible show!

205
00:12:59,672 --> 00:13:05,892
Your national tour has generated a lot of buzz. People call you the top idol queens. Do you think you live up to the hype?

206
00:13:06,272 --> 00:13:14,452
I mean, it would be conceded to say we're the best idols, but we're trendsetters, so we have a responsibility to keep evolving musically.

207
00:13:14,852 --> 00:13:15,212
Shuri!

208
00:13:15,872 --> 00:13:18,812
Saga's a big deal to us, and we're gonna bring it on.

209
00:13:19,492 --> 00:13:23,512
Iron Frill is gonna prove to everyone that we're one of a kind and beyond compare.

210
00:13:23,512 --> 00:13:27,752
We're better than ever, so get ready to see an amazing performance.

211
00:13:31,752 --> 00:13:37,132
Now that's a star right there. It seems like the top idols from Tokyo really know what they're doing, huh?

212
00:13:37,212 --> 00:13:40,612
Isn't Franshu Shuu performing with them over at the new Saga Arena?

213
00:13:41,012 --> 00:13:46,112
Yeah, they're the opening act. It'd be amazing if they managed to outperform Iron Frill.

214
00:13:46,412 --> 00:13:48,332
I wouldn't place bets on that happening.

215
00:13:48,332 --> 00:13:53,812
Hold on, did she just say they're one of a kind and beyond compare?

216
00:13:54,032 --> 00:13:57,452
So she's basically insulting the opening act as a declaration of war!

217
00:13:57,572 --> 00:13:59,192
I'll make her choke on those words!

218
00:13:59,532 --> 00:14:01,132
Kinda doubt she knows us.

219
00:14:01,392 --> 00:14:05,992
Iron Frill is an absurdly famous idol group. It's natural for them to be confident.

220
00:14:06,912 --> 00:14:11,032
If Iron Frill brings their A-game as promised, and if they perform on another level,

221
00:14:11,592 --> 00:14:16,872
people will think we're nothing more than third-rate wannabes, and we'll never be able to get our revenge.

222
00:14:18,332 --> 00:14:28,752
This is how you type.

223
00:14:31,692 --> 00:14:32,872
That's not right!

224
00:14:34,612 --> 00:14:35,812
What do I do?

225
00:14:35,812 --> 00:14:49,812
Sorry, guys. I had to work late today, and...

226
00:14:49,812 --> 00:14:51,812
this is how they feel better.

227
00:14:51,872 --> 00:14:55,652
So, I dream time...

228
00:15:11,932 --> 00:15:12,412
Go!

229
00:15:12,412 --> 00:15:19,652
Saga!

230
00:15:22,652 --> 00:15:23,952
Did you like that?

231
00:15:24,412 --> 00:15:26,432
Did I like what?

232
00:15:26,612 --> 00:15:28,612
I thought our routine could use a little something extra

233
00:15:28,612 --> 00:15:30,952
so we can go out with a bang at the Saga Arena.

234
00:15:32,072 --> 00:15:33,152
Junko, check it out!

235
00:15:33,332 --> 00:15:35,072
Even Tai's getting into the groove.

236
00:15:38,972 --> 00:15:40,292
Whoa, okay, but

237
00:15:40,292 --> 00:15:43,592
we should probably be focusing on the song and dance moves first.

238
00:15:43,592 --> 00:15:45,232
Yeah, of course we'll do that too.

239
00:15:45,872 --> 00:15:48,372
But there's not a whole lot of time left before the concert,

240
00:15:48,752 --> 00:15:50,452
so we thought we'd try something fresh

241
00:15:50,452 --> 00:15:52,232
to leave a big impression on the audience.

242
00:15:52,672 --> 00:15:54,672
It's bad enough without I being here,

243
00:15:55,152 --> 00:15:57,012
so we gotta dig ourselves out of this grave

244
00:15:57,012 --> 00:15:58,992
or we'll have another disaster on our hands.

245
00:16:00,512 --> 00:16:01,312
What's wrong?

246
00:16:02,212 --> 00:16:04,152
Does the routine need something extra?

247
00:16:05,192 --> 00:16:06,652
It's not that exactly.

248
00:16:07,292 --> 00:16:09,232
Awesome, so you want in on this party?

249
00:16:10,292 --> 00:16:14,212
I just need some more time to think about it.

250
00:16:14,832 --> 00:16:15,792
You do that.

251
00:16:16,452 --> 00:16:17,712
Okay, well try it again,

252
